# PyQt Panel + Button Visual Standards (Photo-Derived)

## Atmosphere (Must Match)
- Visual tone must be calm, premium, architectural, and data-focused; avoid playful or saturated UI.
- Keep high clarity with soft surfaces, thin separators, and restrained green accent.
- Use mostly neutral grays + warm white base; accents are sparse and purposeful.

## Core Color Tokens (Exact Hex)
- `BG_APP = #EDEFF2` (window background outside main shell)
- `BG_SHELL = #F6F7F4` (main app container)
- `BG_PANEL = #FBFBF9` (card/box widgets)
- `BG_PANEL_SUBTLE = #F2F3EF` (nested box sections)
- `BORDER_SOFT = #DADDD6` (default panel stroke)
- `BORDER_STRONG = #C8CCC4` (active/selected panel stroke)
- `TEXT_PRIMARY = #161A16`
- `TEXT_SECONDARY = #62685F`
- `TEXT_MUTED = #8B9088`
- `ACCENT_GREEN = #CFE5B8` (progress/focus accent)
- `ACCENT_GREEN_DARK = #9CB77E` (active accent edge)
- `BTN_DARK_TOP = #2E3130` and `BTN_DARK_BOTTOM = #1E201F` (primary CTA gradient)

## Panel / Box Widget Rules (`QFrame`, `QGroupBox`, container widgets)
- Border radius must be `14px` for primary cards, `10px` for nested cards.
- Border width must be `1px`; never remove border on light cards.
- Default panel style:
  - background: `BG_PANEL`
  - border: `1px solid BORDER_SOFT`
- Selected/focused panel style:
  - background: `BG_PANEL`
  - border: `1px solid BORDER_STRONG`
- Internal padding for panel content must be `16px` (primary) or `12px` (nested).
- Horizontal gap between sibling panels must be `12px`; vertical gap `10px`.
- Do not use saturated shadows. If shadow is used, only `rgba(0,0,0,0.08)` blur <= `16`.

## Button Rules (`QPushButton`)
- Button height must be `36px` minimum for secondary actions, `40px` for primary CTA.
- Border radius must be `9px` (secondary) or `10px` (primary).
- Text must be semibold (weight `600`) and centered.

- Primary CTA (`Run`, `View`, `Start`):
  - background: vertical gradient `BTN_DARK_TOP -> BTN_DARK_BOTTOM`
  - text: `#F2F4F1`
  - border: `1px solid #222524`
  - hover: increase brightness by ~6% (top `#383C3A`, bottom `#272A29`)
  - pressed: darken by ~8% (top `#262928`, bottom `#171918`)
  - disabled: background `#B8BCB6`, text `#ECEEEA`, border `#AEB3AC`

- Secondary / neutral buttons:
  - background: `#F3F4F1`
  - text: `TEXT_PRIMARY`
  - border: `1px solid BORDER_SOFT`
  - hover: background `#EEF0EB`, border `#C9CDC5`
  - pressed: background `#E4E7E1`, border `#BCC1B9`
  - disabled: background `#F0F1EE`, text `#A0A59E`, border `#D8DBD4`

## Typography + Line Rules
- Use one sans-serif family consistently (`Inter`, `Segoe UI`, or `SF Pro Text` fallback).
- Page title: `48-56px`, section title: `28-32px`, card title: `16-18px`, body/value: `13-15px`.
- Separator lines must be `1px` and `#E3E5E0`; avoid heavy dividers.

## Strict Prohibitions
- No bright blue default Qt focus rings; replace with `ACCENT_GREEN` or subtle gray focus state.
- No pure white (`#FFFFFF`) for large surfaces except tiny chips/badges.
- No button colors outside defined tokens for primary/secondary states.
- No inconsistent radius values outside `10px` and `14px` for panel system.

## Acceptance Checklist
- Every visible panel matches border, radius, and padding rules.
- Every button has defined `default + hover + pressed + disabled` style.
- UI reads as calm premium dashboard, not generic Qt template.
